NO NEED TO RUN SCRIPTS AT THE MOMENT—ALL THREE FILES HAVE ALREADY BEEN COMBINED INTO final.csv.
The individual files also exist separately and they have .xlsx extensions.

All scripts simply need to be executed from this folder. Based on the .xlsx files (which are public registers downloaded from data.gov.rs), they will automatically generate the corresponding .csv files.

BEFORE running ResultsForSanitaryUnsanitary, open the script and adjust the filename to match the specific file for which you want to generate the final CSV.

Final CSV: contain all calculated and required data.
xlsx files: contain only basic information.
EXECUTION ORDER:

Run TypeToCSV for all three files.
Run ResultsForWild
Run ResultsForSanitaryUnsanitary twice, changing the input filenames accordingly.
Run CombineAll.
Run Formatting.
Run AddingTiles.
Run DeletingExtensions.

All finished data is located in the registryLandfills.csv
